This package contains two things under that license: the Swift wrapper in
Sources/Newtua, and — inside the XCFramework attached to each release — the
compiled newtua-ffi library, and through it the newtua-core engine. The
engine's legacy-format decoders are ported from XADMaster (© Dag Ågren and
contributors, GNU LGPL), which is where the license comes from.

The Lesser GPL is what makes this workable for applications: an app may link
this package, embed the framework and remain under a license of its own
choosing. What the LGPL asks in return is that users be able to replace the
library itself — which dynamic linking, used here, already provides.

RAR support and the UnRAR license. RAR archives are read through libunrar, by
way of the newtua-unrar fork. The UnRAR sources are not part of this
repository, but their object code is compiled into the XCFramework attached to
each release. They carry a license of their own (© Alexander Roshal) that
permits use in any software handling RAR archives, but forbids using the code
to build a RAR-compatible archiver.

That restriction reaches no user of this software. newtua never creates
archives — it extracts and lists only — so no RAR compressor can be derived
from it. The combination is conveyed under section 4 of the LGPL v3, which
permits a Combined Work under other terms provided the library is identified
and its license supplied. The UnRAR license text is in UNRAR-LICENSE.txt.

